       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for ibuprofen is 3,200 mg/day for inpatients, and 1,200 mg/day is the usual OTC limit.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n\nAt this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury and cardiovascular events go up a lot. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **400 mg** by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day) for mild to moderate pain\n- **600 mg** by mouth four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day), or four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the ceiling)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll reconsider. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away."
